# TARGET ARCHITECTURE: x86_64 | v0.18 | azure/ubuntu2204
# Enterprise Linux Audit v0.18  |  [azure/ubuntu2204]
# Tier: tier-1-baseline
# Purpose: MAC administrative policy changes and enforcement context
# Source/authority: DISA applicable product STIG/SRG as applicable; vendor SELinux/AppArmor docs
# Architecture: x86_64 (b64 native, b32 compatibility); use aarch64/ subprofile for ARM64.
# Release state: engineering candidate; NOT independently certified STIG compliant.


# AppArmor policies; AppArmor denials are logged through audit/journal/syslog as configured.
-a always,exit -F arch=b64 -F dir=/etc/apparmor.d -F perm=wa -k t1_apparmor_policy
# AppArmor parser is ACTIVE as a V2R10 requirement; ensure the binary exists before loading.
# Ubuntu 22.04 package manifest lists /sbin/apparmor_parser; applicable 22.04
# Source: https://packages.ubuntu.com/jammy/all/apparmor/filelist
# UBTU-22-654010 / V-260604 | V2R10 published check/fix mapping; path/package prerequisites still require image validation
-a always,exit -F path=/sbin/apparmor_parser -F perm=x -F auid>=1000 -F auid!=unset -k t1_apparmor_parser
# Active executable watch: if the binary is absent, resolve by package prerequisite or an approved waiver.

# the binary is absent install apparmor or document an approved exception.
